  "content": {
    "title": "Where to Stream the 2026 iHeartRadio Music Awards Online Without Cable",
    "text": "If you purchase an independently reviewed product or service through a link on our website, Rolling Stone may receive an affiliate commission.The iHeartRadio Music Awards are back on Thursday to highlight music’s most popular artists and their biggest hits. The star-studded thirteenth annual awards show will be held at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood and will feature performances from the likes of Alex Warren and Kehlani, plus appearances from A-listers like Taylor Swift and other nominees. The show will be hosted by Grammy-winner Ludacris.More from Rolling StoneAt a Glance: Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026TV channel: FoxDate, start time: Thursday, March 26 at 8 p.m. ET get free trial at directv The 2026 iHeartRadio Music Awards will be televised on Fox, but viewers without cable can still tune in using a handful of live TV streaming services. Read on for a full guide on where to stream the iHeartRadio Music Awards.Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026 OnlineBelow are four of the best live TV streaming services that you can use to watch the iHeartRadio Music Awards online without cable.Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026 Online Without CableDirecTV get free trial ➤ Five-day free trial➤ Fox in MyNews, MySports, and all Signature Packages➤ $39.99 a month after trialDirecTV is our favorite live TV streaming service because it offers a large selection of packages for different viewing needs and budgets, and it comes with a five-day free trial (use that to stream the iHeartRadio Music Awards for free). Packages with Fox include the MyNews and MySports Genre Packs and all of the larger Streaming Packages. The most affordable plan (after the free trial ends) is the MyNews Genre Pack at $39.99 a month.Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026 Online Without CableBEST FOR SPORTSFubo get free trial ➤ Five-day free trial➤ Fox in all plans➤ Starting at $55.99 a month after trialAnother one of the best overall live TV streaming services is Fubo, which carries Fox in all of its plans. Packages start at $55.99 a month, but you get a five-day free trial and up to $30 off your first month’s bill.Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026 Online Without CableSling Sign up ➤ Fox in Select, Blue, and Orange + Blue plans➤ Starting at $19.99 a month➤ No free trialSling carries Fox in its Select, Blue, and Orange + Blue packages. These plans start at just $19.99 a month (for Select), making it very affordable. However, Sling does not offer a free trial like the other options on this list.Where to Stream iHeartRadio Music Awards 2026 Online Without CableHulu + Live TV get free trial ➤ Three-day free trial➤ $89.99 a month after trialHulu + Live TV includes Fox in its lineup of 90+ channels and offers a three-day free trial to start. The service is more pricey at $89.99 a month, but you also get Disney+, ESPN, and Hulu’s on-demand library included in that price.iHeartRadio Music Awards Start Time, Date 2026The 2026 iHeartRadio Music Awards will be broadcast on Thursday, March 26 at 8 p.m. ET.iHeartRadio Music Awards Nominees, Taylor Swift AppearanceTaylor Swift enters the 2026 iHeartRadio Music Awards with the most nominations, and she’ll be making a highly anticipated appearance at the show. Swift’s nine nominations are for artist of the year, song of the year, pop song of the year, favorite TikTok dance, best lyrics, best music video, favorite on screen, and favorite tour style.Other artists with multiple nominations include Bad Bunny, BLACKPINK, j-hope, KATSEYE, Kendrick Lamar, Lady Gaga, Linkin Park, Morgan Wallen, Carpenter, SZA, Tate McRae, and Twenty One Pilots, among others.Miley Cyrus, who’s fresh off the Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special, will also appear at tonight’s awards show to receive the Innovator Award. This year’s Icon Award will be given to John Mellencamp.Use one of the streaming services above to watch the iHeartRadio Music Awards online and catch all the artists in attendance.Best of Rolling StoneSign up for RollingStone's Newsletter. For the latest news, follow us on Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram.",
